2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1060) 'A thirdparty/ reset
 # uuid: daea5ab9-1121-5513-90dd-0caa800f0496
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Committed  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1060) 'the repository root
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Two moves make the browser client a dependency and the API server the repository root.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1060) '108 files outside `src/library/` still imported from it, and RFD66606-1023's per-file move rule gave no place to put those files a port did not cover yet.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Put new work at the repository root, and compose with `thirdparty/3d_studio/` through a port per RFD66606-1023, or leave it alone.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1060) 'A thirdparty/ reset
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Two moves, one after the other. First, `src/library/` to `thirdparty/library/`, as real files and not a symlink. Second, `weftspun_studio/` becomes the repository root, and everything that was at the root moves to `thirdparty/3d_studio/` instead.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1060) 'RFD66606-1019 gives the strangler fig this reset makes room for. RFD66606-1023 gives the per-file move rule this RFD does not replace. RFD66606-1057 tracks two items this move left open. RFD66606-1058 gives the Quadlet paths this RFD updates.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Why a dependency directory
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Gall's law: a complex system that works grew from a simple system that worked. Moving the browser client to `thirdparty/` marks it a dependency, not the workspace.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1060) 'The symlink attempt, and why it failed
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1060) 'The first attempt at moving `src/library/` left a symlink at `src/library`. A working session found that symlink broke relative imports inside the moved files. Vite resolves a symlink to its real path before applying a relative import. So `thirdparty/library/aiModelsCatalog.js`'s `import '../core/domain/catalog.js'` resolved against `thirdparty/core/`, which does not exist, instead of `src/core/`, which does. `resolve.preserveSymlinks: true` in `vite.config.js` and `vitest.config.js` fixed it once. Then a direct instruction reversed the symlink call: move the real files.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1060) 'The second move, in full
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1060) '`weftspun_studio/` becomes the repository root. Everything that was at the root, `src/`, `package.json`, `vite.config.js`, `index.html`, `public/`, `native/`, `tests/`, and the JS toolchain's own `scripts/*.mjs` files, moves to `thirdparty/3d_studio/`. `decisions/`, `.github/`, and a small, named set of root-level `scripts/` stay at the root, alongside `weftspun_studio/`'s promoted `lib/`, `test/`, `config/`, `mix.exs`, `Dockerfile`, and `deploy/`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1060) 'New work happens at the root: in `lib/`, in `thirdparty/3d_studio/src/core/`, or in `thirdparty/3d_studio/src/chain/`. It composes with `thirdparty/3d_studio/` through a port, per RFD66606-1023, or it does not touch it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Why a real move, not a rewrite of every import
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1060) 'RFD66606-1057 says a sweep is the wrong shape for a large, low-value change. "Convert one when its model is next worked on, and not in a sweep," in RFD66606-1057's own words. RFD66606-1023 says the same rule for `src/library/`. "A module moves when a port covers it, and not before."
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Neither RFD66606-1023's per-file rule, nor RFD66606-1057's no-sweep rule, required rewriting relative imports inside the moved trees. `git mv` preserves history. Every existing import between files that moved together keeps its shape. Those files moved as one tree, not as 139 and then several hundred independent edits.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1060) 'What stays at the root, and why
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1060) '**`decisions/`**, direct instruction. The RFD index documents both `weftspun_studio` and the browser client. Splitting it would break RFD66606-1000's DRY policy.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1060) '**`.github/`**, GitHub Actions only discovers workflows at the true repository root. It cannot move.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1060) '**`.devcontainer/`**, RFD66606-1056's dev container, for the Elixir side. `devcontainer.json` sets `privileged: true` and `--cgroupns=host` specifically so Quadlet units can start inside it. Removed in this session, ahead of a rebuild.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1060) '**Six `scripts/` files, at the time of this move**, `ci.sh`, `deploy-weftspun-quadlet.sh`, `studio-test.sh`, `check-elixir-parses.exs`, `ste-lint-decisions.py`, `check-model-images.py`. `.pre-commit-config.yaml` named four of these by path, and pre-commit hooks run from the repository root.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Every other file under the old `scripts/` moved to `thirdparty/3d_studio/scripts/` instead. That set is the JS build helpers, the DGX sync scripts, and the XR proxies. Those files read and write that tree, not this one. RFD66606-1063 later deleted `ste-lint-decisions.py`, leaving five.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1060) '**`LICENSE`, `TRADEMARKS`, `.formatter.exs`, `.gitattributes`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`**, repository-wide, not app-specific. `.formatter.exs` now merges two input globs that used to be two files: `decisions/**/*.{ex,exs}` (from the root's old file) and `{mix,.formatter}.exs`, `{config,lib,test}/**/*.{ex,exs}` (from `weftspun_studio/`'s).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Paths this move touched
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1060) '`WeftspunStudio.JsCatalog.@default_path`, `test/catalog_parity_test.exs`, and `test/fact_store_test.exs` read `thirdparty/3d_studio/src/library/aiModelsCatalog.js` now, in place of `../src/library/aiModelsCatalog.js`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1060) '`deploy/quadlet/weftspun.build` and `weftspun-crdb.build` read `/opt/weftspun/src/Dockerfile` and `/opt/weftspun/src/deploy/Dockerfile.crdb` now, in place of the `weftspun_studio/` prefix RFD66606-1058 wrote. `scripts/deploy-weftspun-quadlet.sh` still syncs the whole repository to `/opt/weftspun/src`, and that tree's root is this repository's root.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1060) '`package.json`'s `lint:ste` script read `../../scripts/ste-lint-decisions.py` and `../../decisions/0*/README.md` at the time of this move, because `package.json` lives two levels under the tree those two paths were actually in. RFD66606-1063 later deleted that script and that npm entry.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1060) '`.pre-commit-config.yaml`'s `studio-test` hook matches `^(lib|test|config)/.*\.exs?$|^mix\.exs$` now, in place of `^weftspun_studio/.*\.exs?$`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1060) 'Verified
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1060) '`mix compile` and `mix test` ran clean from the new root, at the time of this move: 100 of 105 tests passed, 5 excluded. The 5 failures were a pre-existing architecture mismatch, unrelated to this move. `deps/taskweft_nif/priv/libtaskweft_nif.so` was an ARM aarch64 binary, and this box is x86_64. `file` on the `.so` confirmed it, and the failure was identical with or without the swap. RFD66606-1057 records the later fix. All 105 tests pass now.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1060) '`npx vitest run` from `thirdparty/3d_studio/` resolves `src/library/aiModelsCatalog.js`'s `import '../core/domain/catalog.js'` correctly, now that `library/` is a real directory under `src/` again, and not a symlink elsewhere. `src/core` and `prepareGlbForApiUpload.test.js` together: 54 passed, the same 5 pre-existing `glbCompress.js` export failures RFD66606-1023 already records, and no import-resolution failure.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1060) 'What this does not do
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1060) 'It does not fix the `prepareGlbForApiUpload` gap RFD66606-1023 already records. That gap sits inside `thirdparty/3d_studio/src/library/glbCompress.js` now, the same as it sat inside `src/library/glbCompress.js` before.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1060) 'It does not touch RFD66606-1023's `src/core/` / `src/chain/` split. Both trees moved together, under `thirdparty/3d_studio/src/`, with every import between them intact.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1060) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1060) '`src/library/` held 139 files and 56,376 lines. It predates RFD66606-1019's strangler fig and RFD66606-1023's `src/core/` split.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1060) 'The repository root carried the same problem at a larger scale. `weftspun_studio/` sat as a subdirectory of the browser client's tree, even though RFD66606-1019 makes it the API server the client is one consumer of. The end-shape system was the guest. The system it replaces was the host.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1060  1 LINE
 Text:Written
